%N A038746 Number of equivalence classes under rotations and reflections of non-straight n-step self-avoiding walks on the square lattice having no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A038746 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026: (Start)
%C A038746 Previous name was: Coefficients arising in the enumeration of configurations of linear chains.
%C A038746 Rotations and reflections act on the ordered vertex sequence; reversal is not included, so the start and end remain distinguished.
%C A038746 (End)
%C A038746 From _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 01 2019: (Start)
%C A038746 Nemirovsky et al. (1992), for a d-dimensional hypercubic lattice, define C_{n,m} to be "the number of configurations of an n-bond self-avoiding chain with m neighbor contacts." For d=2 (square lattice) and m=0 (no neighbor contacts), we have C(n, m=0) = A173380(n). These values (from n=1 to n=11) are listed in Table I (p. 1088) in the paper.
%C A038746 According to Eq. (5), p. 1090, in the above paper, for a general d, the partition number C_{n,m} satisfies C_{n,m} = Sum_{l=1..n} 2^l*l!*Bin(d,l)*p_{n,m}^{(l)}, where the coefficients p_{n,m}^{(l)} (l=1,2,...) are independent of d. For d=2 (square lattice), this becomes C_{n,m} = Sum_{l=1..n} 2^l*l!*Bin(2,l)*p_{n,m}^{(l)}.
%C A038746 According to Eq. (7a) and (7b), p. 1093, in the paper, p_{n,0}^{(1)} = 1 = p_{n,0}^{(n)}, p_{n,m}^{(1)} = 0 for m >= 1, and p_{n,m}^{(l)} = 0 for m >= 1 and n-m+1 <= l <= n.
%C A038746 Now, assume d=2. Since p_{n,0}^{(1)} = 1 for n >= 1, we have C_{1,0} = 2^1*1!*Bin(2,1)*1 = 4, while C_{n,0} = 4 + 2^2*2!*Bin(2,2)*p_{n,0}^{(2)} = 4 + 8*p_{n,0}^{(2)} for n >= 2. The partition numbers p_{n,0}^{(2)} appear in Table II, p. 1093, in the paper. For the current sequence, we have a(n) = p_{n,0}^{(2)} (with a(1) = p_{1,0}^{(2)} = 0 to make the formula A173380(n) = C_{n,0} = 4 + 8*p_{n,0}^{(2)} = 4 + 8*a(n) valid even for n=1).
%C A038746 Apparently, some of the numbers C_{n,m} (for d=2 and d=3) are calculated in Fisher and Hiley (1961); see Table II, p. 1261 (square and cubic). For d=2, they calculate C(n,0) for 1 <= n < 14, while for d=3, they calculate C(n,0) for 1 <= n <= 10. It seems, however, that there are some possible typos there. The typos (for both d=2 and d=3) become apparent if one compares their results with the numbers in Table I (p. 1088) in Nemirovsky et al. (1992). See the comments for A173380 for more details.
%C A038746 (End)
%C A038746 The terms a(12)-a(32) are independently confirmed by Table B1 (pp. 4738-4739) of the published version of Bennett-Wood et al. (1998), corresponding to Table 4 (pp. 26-28) in Appendix B of the arXiv version. In the authors' notation, c_n(0) = C_{n,0}, and the table gives c_n(0)/4 = 2*a(n) + 1. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026
%H A038746 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1088/0305-4470/31/20/010">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, J. Phys. A: Math. Gen. 31 (1998), 4725-4741.
%H A038746 D. Bennett-Wood, I. G. Enting, D. S. Gaunt, A. J. Guttmann, J. L. Leask, A. L. Owczarek, and S. G. Whittington, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9803359">Exact enumeration study of free energies of interacting polygons and walks in two dimensions</a>, arXiv:cond-mat/9803359 [cond-mat.stat-mech], 1998.
%H A038746 M. E. Fisher and B. J. Hiley, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1731729">Configuration and free energy of a polymer molecule with solvent interaction</a>, J. Chem. Phys., 34 (1961), 1253-1267.
%H A038746 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108; see Eq. 5 (p. 1090).
%F A038746 a(n) = (A173380(n) - 4)/8 = (A182644(n+1) - 2)/4 for n >= 1. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026
%e A038746 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 05 2026: (Start)
%e A038746 a(1) = 0 because every 1-step walk is straight and hence excluded.
%e A038746 a(2) = 1. There are 12 two-step self-avoiding walks starting at a fixed lattice vertex. Every such walk has no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice. Four are straight and are excluded; the remaining eight form one equivalence class under rotations and reflections, represented by
%e A038746     S---o
%e A038746         |
%e A038746         X
%e A038746 Thus a(2) = (12 - 4)/8 = 1. Here S marks the start and X the end.
%e A038746 (End)
%Y A038746 Cf. A173380 (corresponding rooted walks), A182644 (fixed snake polyominoes), A001411 (all square-lattice self-avoiding walks), A033155 (d=2, m=1), A033323 (d=2, m=2), A038747 (corresponding coefficient for m=1), A038748 (companion coefficient for m=0), A336492 (total number of contacts).
%Y A038746 Cf. A174319 (d=3, m=0), A034006 (d=4, m=0), A047057 (d=3, m=1), A042949 (d=4, m=1), A049230 (d=3, m=2), A046788 (d=4, m=2).
%Y A038746 Cf. A002932 (erroneous version of A173380), A002934 (erroneous version of A174319).
